This setter is not on the decode path, so no rewrite of it will make decoding measurably faster. The only behavior-preserving change I can make is cosmetic: I pass the defaulted arguments explicitly as unsigned literals and add `final`-free inline-friendly braces. The call and its result are unchanged.

```cpp
    void SetPrecipitationProbability(FIT_UINT8 precipitationProbability)
    {
        SetFieldUINT8Value(5U, precipitationProbability, 0U, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```